  "answer": "You can define a request body using a Pydantic model in FastAPI by declaring the parameter as `Body` and defining the Pydantic model with the fields you want to receive. For example, you can use the following code snippet from [tutorial/body-9]:\n\n```python\nfrom fastapi import FastAPI, Body\nfrom pydantic import BaseModel\n\napp = FastAPI()\n\n@app.post(\"/items/\")\nasync def create_item(item: Item = Body(...)):\n    return item\n```\n\nIn this example, `Item` is a Pydantic model with fields `name`, `description`, `price`, and `tax`. The `Body(...)` decorator is used to indicate that the `item` parameter should be taken from the request body.",
